The green skills action programme will cover:

- Green skills training for trainees and job seekers in areas such as renewable energy, energy efficiency, electric vehicles, circular economy, and environmental and resource management;
- Skills training for employees in existing sectors to develop green skills as part of the transition towards a low-carbon economy;
- The implementation of a green skills certification system;
- Training for green skills trainers and assessors.

The remaining €56 million will be spent on digital skills actions, and will provide:

- Training to support the re-skilling and upskilling of people in jobs at risk of being impacted by digitalisation;
